    "narrative": "For LawDog today, we are leaning heavily into players with high-leverage platoon advantages and favorable matchup profiles to offset our missing core talent. Our top play is **Lawrence Butler** (71.26), who benefits from a high-run-environment park and a strong platoon split against P\u00e9rez. He is neck-and-neck with **Bryson Stott** (71.23) and **Taylor Ward** (71.19). While **Bryson Stott** is facing a pitcher in Avila who allows a 5.01 xERA, his score is slightly suppressed by the \"Elite Hold\" warning, which limits his stolen base upside; conversely, **Taylor Ward** offers superior reliability against the lefty Lodolo, making him a cornerstone of today's scoring projection.\n\nThe decision to bench **Drew Gilbert** (50.86) was our tightest call, as he nearly usurped **Gavin Sheets** (51.06) or **Daulton Varsho** (52.12). Although **Drew Gilbert** gains massive value from the park and the slow delivery of the opposing pitcher\u2014which usually signals a green light for our stolen base-focused strategy\u2014the optimizer favored the higher-order protection and positional floor of the starters. We are also monitoring the matchup for **Luis Arraez** and **Jung Hoo Lee**, who both enjoy a significant park adjustment of +14%. While they face a tougher-than-average arm in Gordon, their speed profiles and spot at the top of the order make them essential for maintaining our 5x5 Roto pace. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remaining on the IL and **Yainer Diaz** and **Tyler Freeman** out of today's lineup, we are operating with a lean squad; keep a close eye on the weather and late lineup shuffles for **Cal Raleigh**, who needs a clean game to deliver on his 63.15 score.",
